---
---

<div id="panel-connect" class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 py-4 lg:py-10">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_1fr] gap-8 lg:gap-14 items-center">
    <!-- Left: Hero copy -->
    <div class="space-y-5 text-center lg:text-left">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-wxm-storm/40 border border-wxm-cloud/20 text-wxm-cloud text-xs font-medium">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 animate-pulse"></span>
        <span class="font-semibold text-white">Official WG1200 Gateway Switcher</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl xl:text-[2.6rem] font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight leading-tight">
        Convert your WeatherXM WG1200 gateway in to a <span class="text-wxm-zenith">tri-protocol mesh gateway</span> or a <span class="text-emerald-400">full Meshtastic node</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-wxm-mist leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto lg:mx-0">
        In WeatherXM mode, your paired weather station can publish to WeatherXM, Meshtastic and MeshCore at the same time. In Full Meshtastic mode, the WG1200 itself becomes a native Meshtastic router/repeater. Switch safely over USB; WeatherXM identity, cloud credentials and the factory recovery slot remain intact.
      </p>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-center lg:justify-start space-x-2 text-xs">
        <span class="indicator-dot-green animate-pulse"></span>
        <span class="text-wxm-cloud font-semibold">Compatible Hardware:</span>
        <a
          href="https://weatherxm.com/stations/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 font-mono font-medium underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors inline-flex items-center gap-1"
        >
          <span>WeatherXM D1/D2 WG1200</span>
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 opacity-80" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Right: Primary action card -->
    <div class="w-full max-w-md mx-auto lg:max-w-none p-6 rounded-card bg-wxm-midnight/90 border-2 border-emerald-500/40 backdrop-blur-md shadow-card space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-5">
        <div class="relative flex-shrink-0">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 blur-2xl pointer-events-none"></div>
          <img
            src="/wg1200-gateway.png"
            alt="WeatherXM WG1200 Gateway"
            class="relative w-24 sm:w-28 h-auto drop-shadow-[0_12px_24px_rgba(0,0,0,0.6)] pointer-events-none select-none"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <span class="text-[11px] font-extrabold text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-widest block">Step 1 — USB Connection</span>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Connect Gateway over USB</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-wxm-mist">Select "USB Serial" in the popup window listing the two ports of WG1200.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Dual USB device tip (compact, expandable) -->
      <details class="group text-left p-3 rounded-lg bg-wxm-abyss/80 border border-wxm-cloud/15 text-xs">
        <summary class="flex items-start gap-2 cursor-pointer list-none select-none text-wxm-cloud">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 text-emerald-400 mt-px" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
          <span class="flex-1 leading-snug">
            <span><strong class="text-white">Select USB Serial</strong> when two ports appear.</span>
            <span class="block text-wxm-cloud/90 mt-0.5">
              If it’s busy or silent, try USB JTAG/serial debug unit.
              <span class="text-wxm-zenith underline underline-offset-2 group-open:hidden">Why?</span>
            </span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <ul class="mt-2.5 space-y-1 text-[11px] text-wxm-cloud pl-6">
          <li><strong class="text-white">USB Serial</strong> (e.g. <span class="text-wxm-wash font-mono text-[10px]">cu.usbserial</span> on Mac / <span class="text-wxm-wash font-mono text-[10px]">CH340</span>) <span class="text-emerald-400 font-semibold">(Recommended)</span> — Hardware UART bridge for flashing &amp; console logs.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">USB JTAG/serial debug unit</strong> (e.g. <span class="text-wxm-wash font-mono text-[10px]">cu.usbmodem</span> on Mac) — Native on-chip USB peripheral.</li>
        </ul>
      </details>

      <div class="flex flex-col items-center space-y-3">
        <button
          id="btn-connect"
          type="button"
          class="w-full py-4 px-6 rounded-control font-black text-base btn-primary-green flex items-center justify-center space-x-3 cursor-pointer active:scale-[0.99] focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-emerald-400 focus:ring-offset-2 focus:ring-offset-wxm-midnight select-none shadow-lg"
        >
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-wxm-abyss" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" />
          </svg>
          <span class="tracking-wide">Connect WG1200 Gateway</span>
        </button>

        <button
          id="btn-connect-manual"
          type="button"
          class="text-xs text-wxm-mist hover:text-white underline underline-offset-4 decoration-wxm-cloud/30 hover:decoration-white transition-colors cursor-pointer"
        >
          Device not appearing? Select serial port manually →
        </button>
      </div>

      <!-- Connection Error Callout -->
      <div id="connect-error-banner" class="hidden text-left p-4 rounded-card border border-wxm-error/40 bg-wxm-error/10 text-white space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex items-start space-x-2.5">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-wxm-error flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/>
          </svg>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-white" id="connect-error-title">Connection Failed</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-wxm-cloud/90 mt-1" id="connect-error-detail"></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="text-[11px] text-wxm-mist bg-wxm-abyss/80 p-3 rounded-control border border-wxm-cloud/10 space-y-1.5">
          <p class="font-semibold text-wxm-cloud">Troubleshooting tips:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
            <li><strong>Two USB devices appear:</strong> Select <strong>USB Serial</strong> (<code>cu.usbserial</code> / <code>CH340</code>). If it fails or is busy, try <strong>USB JTAG/serial debug unit</strong>.</li>
            <li>Ensure no other application (PlatformIO, Arduino IDE, serial monitor) is holding the serial port open.</li>
            <li><strong>Manual Bootloader Mode:</strong> Hold down the <span class="text-white font-semibold">BOOT</span> button on the WG1200 while connecting the USB cable (or while pressing RESET), then release BOOT and click Connect.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
